    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0523" n="515" xml:id="pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/172: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-21T17:00:00+01:00">December 21, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 21—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>528. My telegram 527, December 21, 1 p.m.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d666-f1"/> I find
                    that in an earlier despatch describing the death of Sandri which was printed in
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Corriere Delia Sera</hi> of December 18, and which
                    has just been brought to my attention Barzini reported as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The boats were returning to the ship to get medicines and distilled
                            water when boats full of troops which had been lying wait on the other
                            bank during the bombardment approached the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Panay</hi> which was slowly disappearing under water and opened
                            fire with machine guns on the deserted vessel.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
